# An operand whose only content is a hunkless git block still holds a patch: a
# diff --git line followed by mode lines counts as patch content, while the same
# two mode lines without the diff --git line above them would be refused as
# containing no patch.
#
# patch2 only changes m.sh's mode, so its block runs from the operand's first
# byte to its end with no next block to stop at. Patch1 changes only a.c. The
# report must show a.c's edit on patch1's side and m.sh's mode change on
# patch2's side.
bin: DIFFOFDIFFS
args: p1.patch p2.patch
exit: 0
